 event on the axis where the density is greatest, at the bounce $t = 0$"}],"hatch":[],"settings":"$a = 1$, $\\phi = 0$, $z = 0$","input":null,"caption":["The plane of $t$ and $\\rho$ ($\\phi = 0$, $z = 0$) of Senovilla's universe ($a = 1$). The metric on it is $\\cosh^4(act)\\cosh^2(3a\\rho)(-c^2dt^2 + d\\rho^2)$, and the factor drops out of the null condition, so the rays are at 45°, each ingoing ray meeting an outgoing one on the axis $\\rho = 0$. No Christoffel symbol turns them out of the plane, so they are null geodesics, and the Kretschmann scalar is finite everywhere on it.","The fluid's world lines are the vertical lines. It contracts before $t = 0$ and expands after it, and its density, $15a^2c^4/(8\\pi G\\cosh^4(act)\\cosh^4(3a\\rho))$, is greatest at the marked event and falls away from it in every direction."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"18aabfb0051dc9c6"},"slices":[{"view":"universe","surface":0,"label":"$act = -1$","version":"7e21ac0cb5717768","lines":[[[0.0,0.1667],[0.5,0.1667]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.1667],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"universe","surface":1,"label":"$act = -0.5$","version":"fef8143abf0eb24e","lines":[[[0.0,0.3333],[0.5,0.3333]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.3333],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"universe","surface":2,"label":"$act = 0$","version":"915bd98f5778a5ae","lines":[[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.5]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.5],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"universe","surface":3,"label":"$act = 0.5$","version":"5020ec2d42b7e896","lines":[[[0.0,0.6667],[0.5,0.6667]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.6667],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"universe","surface":4,"label":"$act = 1$","version":"f7c414dc92de9c99","lines":[[[0.0,0.8333],[0.5,0.8333]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.8333],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}}]}]}}
